        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The <strong>power of quotient rule</strong> states that if we want to raise the quotient <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{x}{y}]</span> to some power <span class=\"math\">[MATH: n,]</span> we must raise the numerator and denominator to the power <span class=\"math\">[MATH: n]</span> as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "The power of quotient rule states that if we want to raise the quotient [MATH: \\dfrac{x}{y}] to some power [MATH: n,] we must raise the numerator and denominator to the power [MATH: n] as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^n=\\dfrac{x^n}{y^n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^n=\\dfrac{x^n}{y^n}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example,</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example,",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^4=\\dfrac{x^4}{y^4}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^4=\\dfrac{x^4}{y^4}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To see why the power of quotient rule is true, let&#x27;s take the above example and work it out again the long way. We get the same result:</p>",
            "readable_text": "To see why the power of quotient rule is true, let's take the above example and work it out again the long way. We get the same result:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: ((x)/(y))^{4}|=; (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y)|=; (x \u22c5 x \u22c5 x \u22c5 x)/(y \u22c5 y \u22c5 y \u22c5 y)|=; (x^{4})/(y^{4})]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: ((x)/(y))^{4}|=; (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y)|=; (x \u22c5 x \u22c5 x \u22c5 x)/(y \u22c5 y \u22c5 y \u22c5 y)|=; (x^{4})/(y^{4})]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The power of quotient rule is just a shortcut for the process above.</p>",
            "readable_text": "The power of quotient rule is just a shortcut for the process above.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nThe power of quotient rule states that if we want to raise the quotient [MATH: \\dfrac{x}{y}] to some power [MATH: n,] we must raise the numerator and denominator to the power [MATH: n] as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^n=\\dfrac{x^n}{y^n}]\n\nContent:\nFor example,\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^4=\\dfrac{x^4}{y^4}.]\n\nContent:\nTo see why the power of quotient rule is true, let's take the above example and work it out again the long way. We get the same result:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: ((x)/(y))^{4}|=; (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y)|=; (x \u22c5 x \u22c5 x \u22c5 x)/(y \u22c5 y \u22c5 y \u22c5 y)|=; (x^{4})/(y^{4})]\n\nContent:\nThe power of quotient rule is just a shortcut for the process above."
      },
