    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nThe power of quotient rule states that if we want to raise the quotient [MATH: \\dfrac{x}{y}] to some power [MATH: n,] we must raise the numerator and denominator to the power [MATH: n] as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^n=\\dfrac{x^n}{y^n}]\n\nContent:\nFor example,\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{x}{y}\\right)^4=\\dfrac{x^4}{y^4}.]\n\nContent:\nTo see why the power of quotient rule is true, let's take the above example and work it out again the long way. We get the same result:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: ((x)/(y))^{4}|=; (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y) \u22c5 (x)/(y)|=; (x \u22c5 x \u22c5 x \u22c5 x)/(y \u22c5 y \u22c5 y \u22c5 y)|=; (x^{4})/(y^{4})]\n\nContent:\nThe power of quotient rule is just a shortcut for the process above.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Using the Power of Quotient Rule with One Fraction\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{2x}{3}\\right)^4.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n[MATH: ((2x)/(3))^{4} = ((2x)^{4})/(3^{4})]\n\nThen, we apply the power rule and simplify:\n\n[MATH: ((2x)^{4})/(3^{4})|=; (2^{4}x^{4})/(3^{4})|=; (16x^{4})/(81)]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: ((\u2212 2x)/(5))^{3} =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 (4x^{3})/(125)]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 (8x^{3})/(125)]\nc. [MATH: (8x^{3})/(125)]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 (8x^{3})/(25)]\ne. [MATH: (8x^{3})/(25)]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nSimplify [MATH: 9((x)/(3))^{3}.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: x^{3}]\nb. [MATH: (x^{3})/(3)]\nc. [MATH: (x^{3})/(27)]\nd. [MATH: 3x^{3}]\ne. [MATH: 9x^{3}]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Using the Power of Quotient Rule with Two Fractions\n\nExample Prompt:\nSimplify [MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{y}{2}\\right)^3 \\left(\\dfrac{2y}{3}\\right)^2.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n[MATH: ((y)/(2))^{3}((2y)/(3))^{2} = (y^{3})/(2^{3}) \u22c5 ((2y)^{2})/(3^{2})]\n\nNext, we apply the power rule:\n\n[MATH: (y^{3})/(2^{3}) \u22c5 ((2y)^{2})/(3^{2})|=; (y^{3})/(8) \u22c5 (2^{2}y^{2})/(9)|=; (y^{3})/(8) \u22c5 (4y^{2})/(9)]\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule and simplify:\n\n[MATH: (y^{3})/(8) \u22c5 (4y^{2})/(9)|=; (4y^{(3 + 2)})/(72)|=; (4y^{5})/(72)|=; (y^{5})/(18)]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: ((2x)/(3))^{2}((3)/(x))^{3} =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (12)/(x^{5})]\nb. [MATH: (1)/(12x)]\nc. [MATH: 12x]\nd. [MATH: (12)/(x)]\ne. [MATH: (x)/(12)]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (4)/(3)((v)/(4))^{2}((3)/(u))^{2} =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (v^{2})/(u^{2})]\nb. [MATH: (v^{2})/(16u^{2})]\nc. [MATH: (9v^{2})/(u^{2})]\nd. [MATH: (3v^{2})/(4u^{2})]\ne. [MATH: (9v^{2})/(16u^{2})]"
